{
  "schema_version": 5,
  "type": "feature",
  "problem": [
    {
      "text": "The Torch reference generated adjacent GPTJ sine/cosine coefficients but applied NEOX split-half rotation, leaving its existing GPTJ rotation helper unused.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_a2c542775282416e81fa3e416c56a7fc"]
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": [
    {
      "text": "The change pairs style-specific coefficient layouts with style-specific rotation helpers and moves reference arithmetic to float before converting results to half.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_fd170c9e76d543ff81989d85272829e9"]
    }
  ],
  "impact": [
    {
      "text": "Adds GPTJ rotation to the reference path, not a new GPT-J model architecture or native kernel. It also introduces an unconditional conversion of optional K that prevents query-only reference calls.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_fd170c9e76d543ff81989d85272829e9", "call_a2c542775282416e81fa3e416c56a7fc"]
    }
  ],
  "source_notes": [
    {
      "text": "Read the initial modules entry and the native-GPTJ entry. They establish the reference implementation's origins and record its previously unused GPTJ helper and incomplete partial-rotation support.",
      "basis": "ancestor",
      "evidence": ["call_0f69ac2376e64006924a9d042d1dccc9", "call_53134a9db20e4850a5fe8b067bbc5878"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The connection to issue #7, “quantizing model: undefined symbol: __cxa_call_terminate,” and closed issue #6, “No ROCm runtime is found, using ROCM_HOME='/usr',” is inferred solely from their rope.py import traceback lines. They describe installation failures, not rotary arithmetic. Issue #29, “Auto-YaRN for Qwen3? Maybe even set it dynamically?”, concerns scaling policy in the same file; that file overlap does not establish motivation for this change.",
      "basis": "inference",
      "evidence": ["call_00a9b5c7f2e744a7b96e4d3f033024a1", "call_d5fc4efec0ff42deaa358b1b4ccf497a", "call_9231e86321674892a908d4cd36b2155e", "call_fd170c9e76d543ff81989d85272829e9"]
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No Torch implementation, CUDA kernel or repository test was executed. The scalar check uses Python double precision, not float intermediates and half rounding.",
    "Whole-tree literal searches establish the inspected repository callers, not dynamic or external consumers."
  ],
  "links": [
    "bcc096667169d8f34c602ce495b372e3fc9afd2b",
    "543c4b27714c6a677a6e714c452d62532f634cff"
  ],
  "chapters": [
    {
      "id": "modules",
      "title": "Style-correct reference RoPE",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "NEOX splits the last dimension into halves and rotates corresponding channels; GPTJ slices even and odd channels and interleaves their rotated values. Both implement (u cos − v sin, v cos + u sin), but with different channel pairings. The new Q/K wrappers reuse the corresponding single-tensor helper for each tensor.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_fd170c9e76d543ff81989d85272829e9", "call_a2c542775282416e81fa3e416c56a7fc"]
        },
        {
          "text": "compute_sincos already duplicated frequency coefficients by concatenation for NEOX and repeat-interleave for GPTJ. Dispatching apply_torch to the matching helper supplies the missing pairing agreement; every non-NEOX style takes the GPTJ branch.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_a2c542775282416e81fa3e416c56a7fc", "call_fd170c9e76d543ff81989d85272829e9"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Position IDs are explicitly converted to float before the frequency outer product. Removing the half conversion retains float coefficients in the reference cache, while Q/K are converted to float for rotation and then to half. Cache expansion still uses 2048-position allocation increments, not a rotary threshold. Non-in-place results are now explicitly half; in-place mode copies those rounded results into the original tensors.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_fd170c9e76d543ff81989d85272829e9", "call_a2c542775282416e81fa3e416c56a7fc"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Whole-tree searches found compute_sincos consumed only by expand_cache, and cached coefficients consumed locally by apply_torch. Renamed application and rotation helpers have no other matched callers. The sole matched direct apply_torch caller is tests/test_rope.py; no RoPE subclass appeared in the whole-tree RoPE search.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_0ce03097da444fe7b4dc2f911769f588", "call_d9a7b21c3edd442a9b071ea5b6216bfe", "call_b7341b21183247e1b529a6dd55da9671", "call_6f933b713f684352b7defce522d6a625", "call_2e07d7a4f90149b1a9e221ba246391fe", "call_cb5a198a6272410d9bafa9f7479e5295"]
        },
        {
          "text": "A scalar transcription for four channels and two distinct angles matched adjacent-pair rotation exactly, differed from the old split-half application by up to 3.2211, and preserved squared norm within 7.11e−15. This checks the pairing algebra, not repository execution.",
          "basis": "execution",
          "evidence": ["call_3afaaec943b64d09af1c281c4d56ca86"]
        },
        {
          "text": "The earlier GPTJ reference mismatch is removed for full-width Q/K inputs. The partial-rotation limitation remains: neither new helper separates an unrotated tail before multiplying by shorter coefficients.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_a2c542775282416e81fa3e416c56a7fc", "call_fd170c9e76d543ff81989d85272829e9"]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "optional-k-conversion",
      "origin": "authoring_observation",
      "status": "suspected",
      "classification": "defect",
      "description": "The new precision conversions bypass the optional-K guards.",
      "trigger": "Call RoPE.apply_torch(q, None).",
      "expected_behavior": "Rotate Q and return a None K through the existing query-only branch.",
      "actual_behavior": "k.float() raises before that branch; the later k.half() is also unconditional. Four existing test shapes supply None K.",
      "locations": [
        {"commit": "6693b5010504364efbfd099fdc839aab971e7708", "path": "exllamav3/util/rope.py", "symbol": "RoPE.apply_torch"}
      ],
      "source_evidence": ["call_fd170c9e76d543ff81989d85272829e9", "call_d9c1694b8c604d8abf23369e12e653a3"],
      "verification": [
        {
          "method": "source_inspection",
          "description": "Whole-parent search found the test helper as the sole direct caller; it supplies optional K without a guard. The diff introduces the dereference before existing None-aware handling.",
          "evidence": ["call_2e07d7a4f90149b1a9e221ba246391fe", "call_d9c1694b8c604d8abf23369e12e653a3", "call_fd170c9e76d543ff81989d85272829e9"],
          "limits": "Not executed; external callers are outside the search."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "reference-test-discarded-results",
      "origin": "authoring_observation",
      "status": "suspected",
      "classification": "defect",
      "description": "The unchanged comparison test discards both implementations' returned tensors.",
      "trigger": "Run test_rope with non-None K so reference conversion can proceed.",
      "expected_behavior": "Compare rotated reference outputs with native outputs.",
      "actual_behavior": "Both calls use the default in_place=False and ignore their returns; assertions compare reproducibly regenerated input tensors. Active parametrization also excludes GPTJ.",
      "locations": [
        {"commit": "6693b5010504364efbfd099fdc839aab971e7708", "path": "tests/test_rope.py", "symbol": "test_rope"}
      ],
      "source_evidence": ["call_d9c1694b8c604d8abf23369e12e653a3", "call_a2c542775282416e81fa3e416c56a7fc"],
      "verification": [
        {
          "method": "source_inspection",
          "description": "Inspected the parametrized test and both methods' allocation/return behavior; the task changes neither test nor in-place default.",
          "evidence": ["call_d9c1694b8c604d8abf23369e12e653a3", "call_a2c542775282416e81fa3e416c56a7fc", "call_fd170c9e76d543ff81989d85272829e9"],
          "limits": "Test weakness established by source inspection, not a measured passing run."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "partial-reference-width",
      "origin": "authoring_observation",
      "status": "suspected",
      "classification": "defect",
      "description": "Partial rotary dimensions remain unsupported by the reference application.",
      "trigger": "Pass full-width Q/K with head_dim=128 and partial_rotary_factor=0.5 to apply_torch.",
      "expected_behavior": "Rotate the first 64 channels and retain the remaining channels.",
      "actual_behavior": "Frequency construction produces 64-wide expanded coefficients, while both style helpers multiply the entire 128-wide tensor, producing incompatible last dimensions.",
      "locations": [
        {"commit": "6693b5010504364efbfd099fdc839aab971e7708", "path": "exllamav3/util/rope.py", "symbol": "RoPE.apply_torch"}
      ],
      "source_evidence": ["call_a2c542775282416e81fa3e416c56a7fc", "call_fd170c9e76d543ff81989d85272829e9"],
      "verification": [
        {
          "method": "source_inspection",
          "description": "Compared frequency construction with both new full-vector helpers. The sole matched direct caller sets partial_rotary_factor=1.0, so the inspected test does not exercise this inherited limitation.",
          "evidence": ["call_2e07d7a4f90149b1a9e221ba246391fe", "call_d9c1694b8c604d8abf23369e12e653a3", "call_a2c542775282416e81fa3e416c56a7fc", "call_fd170c9e76d543ff81989d85272829e9"],
          "limits": "No tensor execution."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Adds adjacent-pair GPTJ reference rotation and float intermediates, but breaks optional-K calls; existing tests neither enable GPTJ nor compare returned outputs."
}
